{"name":"Safari","hex":"#b6a58b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"safari","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A trip into any undeveloped area to see, photograph or to hunt wild animals in their own environment.","A caravan going on a safari."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take part in a safari."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/safari"}],"entries":[{"title":"Safari","blocks":[{"text":"A safari is an overland journey to observe or hunt wild animals, especially in East Africa. The so-called \"Big Five\" game animals of Africa – lion, leopard, rhinoceros, elephant, and Cape buffalo – particularly form an important part of the safari market, both for wildlife viewing and big-game hunting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Sabi_sabi_game_drive.jpg/330px-Sabi_sabi_game_drive.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safari"},{"title":"Safari (web browser)","blocks":[{"text":"Safari is a web browser developed by Apple. It is built into several of Apple's operating systems, including macOS, iOS, iPadOS, and visionOS, and uses Apple's open-source browser engine WebKit, which was derived from KHTML. It is the second most used browser in the world, after Google Chrome."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/71/Safari_Liquid_Glass_icon.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safari_(web_browser)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Ernest_Hemingway_poses_with_water_buffalo%2C_Africa%2C_1953.jpg/500px-Ernest_Hemingway_poses_with_water_buffalo%2C_Africa%2C_1953.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Ernest_Hemingway_poses_with_water_buffalo%2C_Africa%2C_1953.jpg/500px-Ernest_Hemingway